# Improved AMP (0.1.0-experimental): FILTER ATK, DEC and REL read as times on the same curves: 5.0ms at
# 25, DEC and REL 45.0s at 127.
# Screens only: what the envelopes, the overdrive and the pre-fade sound like is in the sound cases.
# The case sets what its references show: the BD track, every value of the page by CC on the auto channel
# and, where a number depends on it, the tempo. The title bar (kit name, tempo, record state) and the status
# line (track level, pattern) are left out of every comparison (`ignore`).
# A value shows as text in place of its label for a while after a knob turn (not after a CC), so every
# screen is taken after a turn of the knob it is about. The AMP and FILTER pages take 3 counts a step.
# Changes the BD track's sound in the active kit and does not put it back.
name: improved-amp-filter-times
state: changes
ignore: 0 0 128 9, 0 55 128 9

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key FLTR
cc 70 0
cc 71 0
cc 72 64
cc 73 1
cc 74 100
cc 75 0
cc 76 0
cc 77 64
nudge D -1 per 3
wait 750
screen zero
expect zero == ref
# The value text of the knob turned before is gone after 2.5 s (measured, emulator): wait it out.
wait 3000
nudge A +25 per 3
wait 750
screen atk25
expect atk25 == ref
wait 3000
nudge B +25 per 3
wait 750
screen dec25
expect dec25 == ref
wait 3000
nudge D +25 per 3
wait 750
screen rel25
expect rel25 == ref
wait 3000
nudge B +42 per 3 x2
nudge B +18 per 3
wait 750
screen dec127
expect dec127 == ref
nudge B +1 per 3
wait 750
screen decover
expect decover == dec127
wait 3000
nudge D +42 per 3 x2
nudge D +18 per 3
wait 750
screen rel127
expect rel127 == ref
# Back to short times.
cc 71 40
cc 73 40
